Good catch 👍 — that error is very common in Power Apps, and it usually means:

> ❌ Section.Value is being used, but Section is not returning a record with a .Value field



Let’s fix it properly based on how your SharePoint lookup works.


---

🔍 WHY THIS ERROR HAPPENS

In SharePoint:

A Lookup column (like Section) can behave differently depending on setup:

Case	What it returns

Lookup to Title	.Value or .Title
Plain text column	just text (no .Value)
Misconfigured	returns error ❌



---

✅ STEP-BY-STEP FIX

🧩 Step 1: Check Your “Section” Column (VERY IMPORTANT)

Go to: 👉 SE Question List

Check column:

Section

Confirm:

Type = Lookup

Source = SE Section List

Display column = Title (or Section Name)



---

🧪 Step 2: Test What Field Works

In Power Apps, try these one by one inside a label:

Test 1:

ThisItem.Section.Value

Test 2:

ThisItem.Section.Title

Test 3:

ThisItem.Section

👉 One of these will work (no error)


---

🔧 STEP 3: FIX YOUR FILTER

Now update your formula depending on what works:


---

✅ MOST COMMON FIX

Gallery_Questions_H.Items =
Filter(
    'SE Question List',
    Section.Title = Dropdown_Section.Selected.Title
)


---

🟡 If using .Value

Section.Value = Dropdown_Section.Selected.Title


---

🟢 SAFEST METHOD (Recommended ⭐)

Use ID instead of text:

Gallery_Questions_H.Items =
Filter(
    'SE Question List',
    Section.Id = Dropdown_Section.Selected.ID
)

👉 This avoids ALL text mismatch issues


---

🚨 WHY .Id IS BEST

✔ No spelling issues
✔ No space issues
✔ Works even if names change
✔ Faster and more reliable


---

🧠 SAME FIX FOR SUPPLIERS

Update this also:

Gallery_Suppliers.Items =
Filter(
    'SE Supplier List',
    Section.Id = Dropdown_Section.Selected.ID
)


---

⚠️ IF STILL ERROR

Then your column might NOT be lookup.

👉 Quick fix:

Delete Section column

Recreate as Lookup

Link to SE Section List



---

✅ FINAL WORKING VERSION (RECOMMENDED)

Questions:

Filter(
    'SE Question List',
    Section.Id = Dropdown_Section.Selected.ID
)

Suppliers:

Filter(
    'SE Supplier List',
    Section.Id = Dropdown_Section.Selected.ID
)


---

🎯 RESULT

✔ No more .Value error
✔ Dynamic filtering works
✔ Your matrix will load correctly


